Package: leaf
Title: Header-Only Leaf Gas Exchange with Explicit Plant Hydraulics
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Isaac", "Towers", , "", "aut",
            comment = "Author of the leaf gas exchange and hydraulics model"),
    person("Daniel", "Falster", , "daniel.falster@unsw.edu.au", c("aut", "cre"),
            comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9814-092X")),
    person("Rich", "FitzJohn", , "", "ctb",
            comment = "Root-finding utilities (uniroot.hpp)")
    )
Maintainer: Daniel Falster <daniel.falster@unsw.edu.au>
Description: A C++ header-only implementation of leaf-level gas exchange in
    which stomatal behaviour emerges from hydraulics rather than an empirical
    conductance model. Farquhar-von Caemmerer-Berry photosynthesis is coupled to
    an explicit soil-root-stem-leaf water transport path, with Weibull
    vulnerability curves for both xylem and roots, multi-layer soil and
    gravitational head, and the operating point is chosen by Sperry-style
    gain-risk profit maximisation over the root-collar water potential. Forward
    -mode automatic differentiation supplies exact derivatives of profit with
    respect to the collar potential. Extracted from the TF24 strategy in the
    'plant' package so that it can be tested, profiled, extended and embedded
    independently. The package ships headers only: there is no compiled code and
    nothing to link against.
